DP  - 2025 Sep 17
TI  - A software pipeline for medical information extraction with large language 
      models, open source and suitable for oncology.
PG  - 313
LID - 10.1038/s41698-025-01103-4 [doi]
LID - 313
AB  - In medical oncology, text data, such as clinical letters or procedure reports, is 
      stored in an unstructured way, making quantitative analysis difficult. Manual 
      review or structured information retrieval is time-consuming and costly, whereas 
      Large Language Models (LLMs) offer new possibilities in natural language 
      processing for structured Information Extraction (IE) from medical free text. 
      This protocol describes a workflow (LLM-AIx) for extracting predefined clinical 
      entities from unstructured oncology text using privacy-preserving LLMs. It 
      addresses a key barrier in clinical research and care by enabling efficient 
      information extraction to support decision-making and large-scale data analysis. 
      It runs on local hospital infrastructure, eliminating the need to transfer 
      patient data externally. We demonstrate its utility on 100 pathology reports from 
      The Cancer Genome Atlas (TCGA) for TNM stage extraction. LLM-AIx requires no 
      programming skills and offers a user-friendly interface for rapid, structured 
      data extraction from clinical free text.
